# Guest image artifacts. One `<sha256>  <url>  <role>` line per artifact; `#`
# starts a comment and the role defaults to `rootfs`.
#
# The build FAILS CLOSED: a line without a 64-char checksum, an unknown role, or
# a download whose hash does not match stops it. This file is the whole supply
# chain for the guest rootfs.
#
# Roles:
#   rootfs   extracted into the guest rootfs (both tiers) — an archive
#   all, dev REFUSED here: packages are the explicit lists in
#            scripts/build-guest-image.sh (base_rpms / dev_rpms), installed with
#            dnf, and the image records what dnf chose in
#            /etc/pabrik-image-rpms. An `apk` manifest cannot be honoured by a
#            Fedora rootfs, so the roles are refused rather than ignored.
#
# The guest distribution is FEDORA MINIMAL, not Alpine. What that buys: a real
# glibc distribution with dnf inside the workspace, and a shell/toolset that
# matches what the product's own tooling expects. What it costs: the rootfs is
# ~128 MiB before any package is added (Alpine's minirootfs is ~8 MiB), so the
# base image is 1 GiB and a workspace disk is a copy of that.
#
# Version pinning: `releases/44/Container/...` is an immutable Fedora release
# path — published release artifacts are never rewritten, the same guarantee the
# Alpine pin relied on. Never use a `latest`/`updates` path here.
2e405ab2b84155c32887f07ed1b259b342acda7547272607c1d18eb7cd1af961  https://download.fedoraproject.org/pub/fedora/linux/releases/44/Container/x86_64/images/Fedora-Container-Base-Generic-Minimal-44-1.7.x86_64.oci.tar.xz  rootfs
